    {
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "- **Cluster** and **Component** select indexed Loki labels. Both support multi-select and **All**.\n- **Level** filters by severity. Choose **All** to see every level.\n- **Search (regex)** is a case-insensitive regular expression matched against the full log line. The default `^` matches every line without highlighting the whole message. Examples: `worker|mqtt`, `panic|traceback`, or a service ID.\n- **Extra LogQL pipeline** appends raw LogQL pipeline stages after the built-in label, level, and search filters. Leave it empty for normal browsing. Examples: `| json` or `| logfmt | duration > 1s`.\n- **Cross-component links:** expand a log line. If it contains a 24-character Oakestra ID, Grafana extracts that ID and shows **Open in...** links in the log details. Selecting one keeps the time range, sets **Search (regex)** to that exact ID, and changes **Component** to the selected target. It is a correlation shortcut: it only returns lines where that target component logged the same ID.\n- Root links search Root-local Loki; Cluster links search that Cluster-local Loki. A link can show no result when the target did not log that ID in the selected time range.\n- Use the time picker in the top-right to scroll back through retained logs. Open the logs panel menu and choose **Explore** to edit the complete LogQL query interactively.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "12.0.0",
      "title": "",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7
      },
      "id": 12,
      "panels": [],
      "title": "Orchestrator logs",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "Loki"
      },
      "description": "LogQL selector and pipeline are built from the dashboard controls. Use the panel menu to open this query in Explore.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 22,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 8
      },
      "id": 3,
      "options": {
        "dedupStrategy": "none",
        "enableLogDetails": true,
        "prettifyLogMessage": false,
        "showCommonLabels": false,
        "showLabels": true,
        "showTime": true,
        "sortOrder": "Descending",
        "wrapLogMessage": true
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "Loki"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "{cluster_id=~\"${cluster_id:regex}\", compose_service=~\"${compose_service:regex}\"} |~ `(?i)(${level_filter:raw})` |~ `(?i)(${search:raw})` ${logql_pipeline:raw}",
          "maxLines": 1000,
          "queryType": "range",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Selected stream \u2014 ${cluster_id:text} / ${compose_service:text}",
      "type": "logs"
    }
  ],
